<topic template="Default" modified="2026-08-12T15:48:19.075-04:00" lasteditedby="rbwin" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="../helpproject.xsd">
  <title translate="true">PRP: Particle Release Point Package Pane</title>
  <body>
    <header>
      <para styleclass="Heading1"><text styleclass="Heading1" translate="true">PRP: Particle Release Point Package Pane</text></para>
    </header>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true">The </text><text styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">PRT: Particle Release Point Package</text><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true"> pane is on the </text><link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="MODFLOW_Features_Tab" styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">MODFLOW Features</link><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true"> tab of the </text><link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="Object_Properties_Dialog_Box" styleclass="Normal" style="font-weight:bold;" translate="true">Object Properties</link><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true"> dialog box.</text></para>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true">This pane is used to specify the starting location(s) of particles in a MODFLOW 6 </text><link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="Particle-Transport" styleclass="Strong" translate="true">Particle Transport</link><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true"> models. MODFLOW 6 allows for multiple </text><link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="PRT-Particle-Tracking-Model" styleclass="Strong" translate="true">Particle Tracking</link><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true"> models in one simulation and multiple </text><link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="PRP-Particle-Release-Point-Pac" styleclass="Strong" translate="true">Particle Release Point Packages</link><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true"> in one </text><link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="PRT-Particle-Tracking-Model" styleclass="Strong" translate="true">Particle Tracking</link><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true"> model. The </text><link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="PRP-Particle-Release-Point-Pac" styleclass="Strong" translate="true">Particle Release Point Packages</link><text styleclass="Normal" translate="true"> to be used is specified in the combo box and the locations of the particles are specified in the lower half of the pane. Note that with DISV grids, some cells may not be rectangular. In such cases, the particle locations will be calculated by projecting a location from a rectangle circumscribing the cell shape to the center of the cell.</text></para>
  </body>
</topic>
